                "title":"My Witchcraft Research Secret Office",
                "describe":"<p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">As a wizard, I have spent a long time researching witchcraft.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">I think it will be amazing when I have an office in the depths of the ocean.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Then I decided to develop it.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">I make a magic barrier at the part of the room that comes into direct contact with water. The magic barrier is also used to extract O2 from the water and drop the CO2 into a bubble.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">I placed 8 magic stones at each corner of the room. The stone line correlation will produce a zone that is protected by a barrier, so it will be possible for me to customize the pressure in the zone.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A room with some bookshelves around it to archive my journal research. There are two soft sofas, the smallest one gives me the experience of sitting on the throne, and the long one is to take a nap after being tired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This room has a teleportation gate that connects with some places that I have registered, for example, one of my rooms in the middle of the city.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">That is a peaceful place, no annoying voice disruption, no stupid questions like \"Do you know how to open network access for dev environments?\"</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Just a romantic date between me and my research topic. Feel like I can optimize my concentration so I can drive my mind into the focus zone.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">You know what, on sunny days. I can see the beauty of the marine habitat directly.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"> </p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">That feels so peaceful. That's kind of therapy.</p>",
